# Opt-in question interpretation and explicit confirmation

Status: DONE
Milestone: Optional assistance for noisy or unwieldy question drafts
Dependencies: 28_QUESTION_DRAFTS.todo, 39_INSTALLED_CLI_ANSWERS.todo, 42_DIRECT_FAST_ANSWERS.todo

## Purpose

An off-by-default toggle asks the provider to interpret the intended question, then accepts an
explicit Yes or correction. Default direct answers retain their no-follow-up behavior.

## Tasks and acceptance

- [x] Add default-off inline toggle and separate interpretation/reply UX without overwriting the original.
- [x] Send fixed task metadata and bounded, explicitly opted-in clarification history only.
- [x] Interpret first; send another request only for an explicit reply or confirmation.
- [x] Keep ordinary answering, tool isolation, capture policy, cancellation and source bounds intact.
- [x] Exercise initial/correction/confirmation, limits, state changes and no-implicit-send with fake providers.
- [x] Update privacy/setup/handbook/diagrams/images/JOURNAL and final source delivery evidence.

